    "Id": "Gear_Attachment_LaserInsulatorQS",
    "Name": "Laser Insulator",
    "Details": "Laser Insulators — Introduced by the Terran Hegemony in 2575, first seen in the SLDF's Chippewa. The laser bays get wrapped in what we call 'aerogel blankets' — a very technical term for 'fancy space wool.' Gives you the thermal capacity of two standard heat sinks at a fraction of the weight. The one small consideration is that it traps the heat right where it's generated rather than distributing it across the chassis. We call that 'localized thermal retention for optimized performance zones.' So, you want one fitted, or are you happy running stock? Because let's be honest, that's a bit embarrassing.",
